<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belanjong pillar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">914</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Blanjong inscription</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Belanjong pillar is an inscribed stone pillar at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanur">Sanur</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bali">Bali</a>, dated to 914 CE. Its text, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> and Old Balinese written in two scripts, records a campaign of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-kesari-warmadewa">Sri Kesari Warmadewa</a>. It is the oldest dated inscription known from Bali and the earliest record of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warmadewa-dynasty">Warmadewa dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belanjong-pillar.jpg" alt="Belanjong pillar" width="320" height="569" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: I Putu Budhi Arya Premana · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blanjong.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
